                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "For a game focused on writing there sure are a lot of spelling errors. Usually small typos (\"inocent\"), but the sentence \"The town looked like a battlefield, but no battle was not fought here\" got stuck in my mind. Considering that the game actually does not have a lot text, those things stand out.\nOther than that, the concept is as unique as the artstyle. If you're looking for that kind of thing, the gameplay and story are good enough to entertain you for 2-3 hours. The puzzles aren't difficult and the keyboard controls could be better, it's probably more comfortable to play with a controller.\nGrab it on sale.",
